# Context hygiene: keep the build context small and stable, but do NOT exclude
# anything a Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# History: `docker/` was excluded to reduce context size, which silently broke
# `COPY docker/lsp.yaml` — and it only failed on a cache miss, so it looked fine
# until someone touched those files. Anything referenced by a COPY/ADD belongs
# outside this list; that is the rule this file now follows.

# --- VCS / caches ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# --- not needed by any image ---------------------------------------------
var
workspace
demo
tests
docs
scripts

# --- local-only config ---------------------------------------------------
.env
# An operator's local LSP catalog overrides; `docker/lsp.yaml` itself is COPYed.
docker/lsp.local.yaml
# Compose consumes this on the host; the image does not need it.
docker/docker-compose.yml

# --- front-end build inputs that must not travel into an image ------------
# `node_modules` and `dist` were reaching the build context, and because the frontend
# Dockerfile copies the project *after* running `npm ci`, the host's `node_modules` silently
# replaced the one installed from the lockfile -- so the image was built from whatever the
# developer happened to have installed, while the log still said `npm ci`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
# Vite reads `.env*` at build time. Excluding them guarantees that a production image carries
# no API base and must be handed one at run time through `AEGIS_API_BASE`/`config.js`.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- docs -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
!README.md
